    },
    "The bar always draws in plain white or black so it stays readable on any wallpaper. Near the high threshold a value counts as critical: it gets a “!” beside it and VoiceOver says so. Set low above high to invert — useful for metrics where a small number is the bad one." : {

    },
    "The protection score and the two highest-priority findings stay free, permanently — including their evidence and what to do about them." : {

    },
    "The refresh interval above controls the fast tier (CPU, GPU, memory, network, disk). These two sliders control the other two tiers — every module assigned to a tier shares that tier's interval, so this is per-tier control, not independently adjustable per module." : {

    },
    "The security and privacy findings below are unaffected — they are read directly from this Mac's current settings, not from history." : {

