    },
    "When on, Sentry periodically asks macOS for this Mac's approximate location (Wi-Fi-based, not precise GPS) and sends the most recent reading to your iPhone the next time it's on the same local network. This only happens while Sentry is running and the Mac is online — it cannot locate this Mac while it's asleep, offline, or Sentry isn't running, and it has no connection to Apple's Find My network." : {

